# No environment variables are required.
#
# TikZ code is generated locally in the browser from the relative positions of
# the elements on the canvas, and previews compile in-browser via TikZJax
# (WebAssembly TeX, vendored under public/tikzjax/). There is no server-side
# rendering, no model provider, and no API key to configure — the app runs as a
# static deployment on any host.
